  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity strengthening program for Caritas Diocesan Offices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This concept note is in response to the Bishops request aimed at supporting a capacity strengthening program for Caritas Sierra Leone by providing the required support,  resources, and training opportunities to  CSL. 
It is within this framework that Caritas Sierra Leone and the CDA focal Persons produced this capacity strengthening program for CSL staff with the following training outcomes;
1.	A review and &#x2018;follow up from BD Training and to receive accompaniment support&#x2019; from the CDAs in terms of developing BD Plans, donor mapping and approach.
2.	A reviewed &#x2018;Organizational MEAL system&#x2019; for Caritas Sierra Leone.
3.	An &#x201c;Improved understanding on the financial management principles and internal controls for sustainable and efficient financial management&#x201d; for Caritas Sierra Leone.
4.	Staff trained in &#x2018;Risk Management, safety and security Planning. 
5.	Staff trained in &#x2018;Disaster Preparedness Plan and management&#x2019; for Caritas Sierra Leone. 
6.	Caritas Sierra Leone &#x2018;Inventory management system and Procurement manual&#x201d; produced.
7.	Updated organizational &#x2018;Policies produced&#x2019; for Caritas Sierra Leone&#x2019;
&#x2022;	The target participants will constitute Caritas Sierra Leone staff in Programs and Operations units in the 4 Diocesan Caritas offices and the National Offices. 
The capacity-strengthening will be &#x201c;participatory learning&#x201d; using &#x201c;tailor-made facilitation&#x201d;.  We will tap on existing expertise from CDAs where possible or outsource where the expertise is not readily available. Training locations will be rotated among the four (4) diocesan Caritas Offices for experience sharing and learning. 
Program Outline:
A.	Capacity Strengthening
1.	Capacity strengthening in Business Development 
2.	MEAL Systems 
3.	Financial Management and Internal Control systems
4.	Procurement, logistics an Supply Chain Management
5.	Risk Management, Safety and Security
6.	Disaster Preparedness and Management
B.	National Office Operational Support 
C.	Organizational Policies Development and Review</narrative>
  </description>
